% Chapter 67 of the tariff (Section XII): prepared feathers and down and
% articles made of feathers or of down; artificial flowers; articles of human
% hair — all four headings (6701 to 6704) and their 8 six-digit subheadings.
% A library: it includes chapter_39.le (and through it gri.le), because
% subheading 6702.10 is "of plastics" in the sense of Chapter 39 note 1 and
% Chapter 39 note 2(q) sends the articles of Section XII out of Chapter 39;
% tariff.le includes it.
%
% Text: HTSUS Revision 23 (2026), Chapter 67 notes 1 to 3 and the terms of
% the headings and subheadings (https://hts.usitc.gov/); Section XII has no
% notes. Section XI note 1(b) and 1(p), Chapter 39 note 2(q), Chapter 54
% note 1 (synthetic textile materials). The subheadings are the six-digit HS
% ones. US Customs rulings name the articles of heading 6704 (wefts, frontals,
% closures, extensions, eyelashes).
%
% How the chapter is read. A good's heading is decided by its family (the
% kind the ruling names: feathers, an artificial flower, worked human hair,
% a wig, a hair extension...), with the notes that take goods out: heading
% 6701 does not cover feathers that are only filling, padding or trimming,
% nor artificial flowers (note 2); heading 6702 does not cover articles of
% glass nor flowers obtained in one piece or assembled otherwise than by
% binding, gluing or fitting (note 3). The subheadings read what the good is
% classified as consisting of (GRI 3(b), gri.le): of plastics (Chapter 39
% note 1) or of other materials for flowers; of synthetic textile materials,
% of human hair or of other materials for wigs and the like, and for the
% synthetic ones, whether the good is a complete wig.
% Chapter 67 note 1 excludes goods of headings outside the model (straining
% cloth of 5911, footwear, headgear, toys and carnival articles, feather
% dusters): a claim that a good belongs there is answered by the office
% (gri.le).
%
% Provenance: every rule and table is labelled and cites the passage it
% encodes; the documents say where their text is (sources/), so the editor
% shows each passage and the verifier checks every quotation.
%
% DISCLAIMER. This program is an example of Logical English. It is provided
% "as is", without warranty of any kind, express or implied, including any
% warranty that it is accurate, complete, up to date or fit for a particular
% purpose. It is not an official reading of the tariff or of the rulings it
% cites, it is not a binding classification ruling, and it is not legal or
% customs advice. Its answers may be wrong: do not rely on them for a real
% import, export or declaration; consult the official texts, the customs
% authority and a qualified professional. Its authors accept no liability for
% any loss or damage arising from its use.

the target language is: prolog.

the templates are:
    *a family* is a family of chapter sixty-seven goods.
    *a good* has feathers or down only as filling, padding or trimming; undefined.
    *a thing* is made of glass; undefined.
    *a good* is obtained in one piece or assembled otherwise than by binding, gluing or fitting; undefined.
    the hair of *a thing* is *a hair*; undefined.
    *a hair* is a hair of the class *a class*.
    the material class of *a good* in heading *a heading* is *a class*.
    the hair article group of *a good* is *a group*.
    the subheading in heading *a heading* for *a class* of *a group* is *a code* under table feathers.

% ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
% GRI 6: the material the subheadings name and, for wigs of synthetic
% textile materials, whether the good is a complete wig. First match: an
% "any" row is the heading's "Of other materials" or "Other".
% ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
% the six-digit subheadings of headings 6701 to 6704
the table feathers is, with first match, with provenance HTSUS General Rules of Interpretation,
        confer "the classification of goods in the subheadings of a heading shall be determined according to the terms of those subheadings and any related subheading notes":
    row | heading | class           | group         | code      | as stated in HTSUS Chapter 67
    f1  | 6701    | any             | any           | "6701.00" | "6701.00.30"
    f2  | 6702    | plastics        | any           | "6702.10" | "Of plastics: 6702.10"
    f3  | 6702    | other materials | any           | "6702.90" | "Of other materials: 6702.90"
    f4  | 6703    | any             | any           | "6703.00" | "6703.00.30"
    f5  | 6704    | synthetic       | complete wig  | "6704.11" | "Of synthetic textile materials: Complete wigs"
    f6  | 6704    | synthetic       | any           | "6704.19" | "6704.19.00"
    f7  | 6704    | human hair      | any           | "6704.20" | "6704.20.00"
    f8  | 6704    | other materials | any           | "6704.90" | "6704.90.00"

the knowledge base chapter 67 includes these resources:
    chapter_39.

